-# The write-once record. Newest first, and nothing here is worked: a librarian
-# reads it and acts elsewhere. Rows dispatch to _notice_<kind> with
-# _notice_generic as the fallback, so a new kind is a new file rather than a
-# case statement — the same dispatch the audit log uses.
.p-3
  %p.text-muted.small.mb-0
    What the repository did — loads, visibility changes, reindexes, and every work published to a community showcase. One row per event; the Digests tab sums each day up.

%nav.px-3.pb-2{'aria-label' => 'Activity kind'}
  = link_to 'All', admin_ledger_path(tab: 'activity'),
    class: "btn btn-sm me-1 #{@kind.blank? ? 'btn-secondary' : 'btn-outline-secondary'}",
    'aria-current': ('page' if @kind.blank?)
  - AdminNotice::ACTIVITY_KINDS.each do |kind|
    - current = kind == @kind
    = link_to Admin::LedgerHelper::KINDS.dig(kind, :label), admin_ledger_path(tab: 'activity', kind: kind),
      class: "btn btn-sm me-1 #{current ? 'btn-secondary' : 'btn-outline-secondary'}",
      'aria-current': ('page' if current)

- if @notices.any?
  .table-responsive
    %table.table.table-borderless.admin-registry-table.ledger-table.ledger-table--activity
      %thead
        %tr
          %th.text-nowrap{scope: 'col'} When
          %th{scope: 'col'} What
          %th{scope: 'col'} Detail
          %th{scope: 'col'} Who
      %tbody
        - @notices.each do |notice|
          - partial = "admin/ledger/notice_#{notice.kind}"
          - resolved = lookup_context.exists?(partial, [], true) ? partial : 'admin/ledger/notice_generic'
          = render partial: resolved, locals: { notice: notice }
  = paginate @notices
- else
  .admin-registry__empty
    %i.fa-solid.fa-book.admin-registry__empty-icon{'aria-hidden' => 'true'}
    %p.mb-1.fw-semibold.text-body Nothing recorded yet
    %p.mb-0.small.text-muted
      Loads, visibility changes, reindexes and showcase publications are recorded here as they happen.
